# Pairs with ReadPositionHonest, and reproduces issue #4467 as production had it
# until #4489 fixed it (the sibling of issue #4451 the
# fix session found: a cold rebuild that faults part-way re-arms its replay
# barrier within the same activation with the partly rebuilt projection still in
# memory, sees a non-empty cache, and resumes WARM from the persisted checkpoint,
# skipping the entries between its re-read frontier and that checkpoint.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestFaultedColdReplayResumesWarm
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a re-armed replay after a cold-rebuild fault resumes from the persisted checkpoint over a partial projection
PERTURBS: ReplayFaultRearm

--- FIND
    /\ rp[l] < anchor[l]
    /\ UNCHANGED vars
--- REPLACE
    /\ rp[l] < anchor[l]
\* MUTATION: the re-armed replay resumes warm from the persisted checkpoint.
    /\ rp' = [rp EXCEPT ![l] = stCp[l]]
    /\ replayRequested' = [replayRequested EXCEPT ![l] = TRUE]
    /\ UNCHANGED walVars
    /\ UNCHANGED <<up, cache, stCp, durCp, anchor, clk, cov, snapCov, snapRows, stale>>
    /\ UNCHANGED pinVars
    /\ UNCHANGED faults
--- END